[RUNNING]● Message: **Updates**
- Parent build now acts as the aggregator for `modules/core-platform`, with the Spotless formatter pointing at `${maven.multiModuleProjectDirectory}` and CI/Sonar artifacts updated to look under the module tree, plus nested Maven `target/` folders are ignored so we no longer commit build output (`pom.xml:5-152`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml:225-301`, `sonar-project.properties:9-31`, `.gitignore:2-3`).
- The npm/Node automation scripts are multi-module aware: project scripts call Maven with `-pl modules/core-platform`, `tools/install.cjs` resolves and compiles that module in parallel-safe fashion, `tools/test.cjs` drives `verify`/JaCoCo against the module and reports its coverage folder, `tools/run.cjs` launches Quarkus dev mode for the module, and `tools/lint.cjs` still outputs JSON-only diagnostics from Spotless (`package.json:28-40`, `tools/install.cjs:19-218`, `tools/test.cjs:18-146`, `tools/run.cjs:15-125`, `tools/lint.cjs:14-158`).
- Documentation now matches the new layout: the README explains the parent/child POM structure and every Maven command example calls out `-pl modules/core-platform`, while all architectural references (java standards, testing strategy, platform/consignor specs, feature-flag governance) point to `modules/core-platform/src/main/webui/...` so contributors know where to work (`README.md:105-174`, `docs/java-project-standards.adoc:530-549`, `docs/testing/strategy.md:65-86`, `CONSIGNOR_PORTAL_IMPLEMENTATION.md:13-37`, `docs/platform/console.md:417-454`, `docs/feature_flags/governance.md:586-590`, `docs/consignor-portal.md:16-42`).
- Recorded completion of I1.T1 in the iteration tracker to unblock dependent tasks (`.codemachine/artifacts/tasks/tasks_I1.json:3-33`).

